## 1.0.0 - 2026-10-28

Initial delivery. The ammo plugin runs an AMMO campaign host-local, inside a
Pumice checkout, on Claude Code or Codex, with no server, container, web UI,
or archive store. It ships the lead skill (`ammo:ammo`) and the report
sub-skill (`ammo:ammo-report`), the role agents for both harnesses, the
campaign hooks, the state schema and transition data, the measurement,
serving, and GPU-lease scripts, and the PAVE graph: 15 nodes and 50 edges
that map the seven stages, four audits, five binding gates, the debate, and
the fact-checked report one to one. One campaign lives at
`<pumice-checkout>/.ammo/<campaign-id>/`. The runtime profile is
`pumice-cuda`; Neuron profiles are refused.
